00:02:24.557 --> 00:02:29.677
Allery farms more than 260 hectares of wheat, corn, soybeans, and hay.

00:02:30.217 --> 00:02:31.657
The farm goes back to his grandfather.

00:02:32.157 --> 00:02:34.957
He asked whether he will lose half his land or his house,

00:02:35.317 --> 00:02:38.797
and said he learned of the project at the start of the year without ever being consulted.

00:02:39.317 --> 00:02:41.337
He called it a project that is not transparent.

00:02:41.997 --> 00:02:43.957
Altow, the federal agency in charge,

00:02:44.277 --> 00:02:46.697
wants high-speed rail between Quebec City and Toronto,

00:02:47.177 --> 00:02:49.237
and much of the mapped route runs on farmland.

00:02:49.737 --> 00:02:54.357
Simon Duval, regional president of the Union Desk Prodoctor's Agricoles in Lano-Dier,

00:02:54.357 --> 00:02:59.637
said farmers have to stop the project now. He said a line that leaves half a farm on the far side

00:02:59.637 --> 00:03:04.937
forces a detour that would ruin the finances of the operation. An alto spokesperson told Global

00:03:04.937 --> 00:03:10.737
News the agency held consultations earlier this year and took 20,000 comments. Near more urban

00:03:10.737 --> 00:03:16.237
places such as Repentany, Alto said, the priority is a route that limits harm to neighborhoods and to

00:03:16.237 --> 00:03:22.297
agricultural land. Patrick Bonan, the Block Kibbequah member for Repentany, said he cannot support the

00:03:22.297 --> 00:03:26.757
project because there is no proper public consultation and no environmental assessment.

00:03:27.217 --> 00:03:31.217
City Councilor Normand Urbain asked people to picture a train through the middle of a

00:03:31.217 --> 00:03:34.897
farm and said tractors cannot cross the rails from one side to the other.

00:03:35.457 --> 00:03:38.037
Allery said he would be losing a piece of his reason to live.

